etymology_text:
Uncertain; perhaps from either Proto-Indo-European:
* *Hedʰ-téh₂-h₁ (“said, announced”), from instrumental of *Hedʰ-téh₂, from *Hedʰ- (“to say”) (whence Sanskrit आह (ā́ha, “to say”), Old Avestan 𐬁𐬛𐬁 (ādā, “to say”)) + *-téh₂;
* *Hedʰ-dh₁-éh₁, from *Hedʰ- (“to say”) + *deh₁- (“to bind”) + *-téh₂;
* *m̥d-dh₁-éh₂, from *med- (“to measure, advise”) + *deh₁- (“to bind”) + *-éh₂;
* or *n̥-h₂n̥dʰ-téh₂ (“unblinded”), from *n̥- (negative prefix) + *h₂endʰ- (“to be blind”) + *-téh₂.
